From a23c79df7b3b8fb21b53838f58c09ba67c6a327f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 07:11:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add the non linear solver of KINSOL

The KINSOL non linear solver (registered when MFEM is built with
SUNDIALS) uses KINSOL through a class derived from mfem::KINSolver:
Newton's method with or without line search, a modified Newton method
(MaximumSetupCalls), and Picard's method, the tangent operator of the
first iteration being kept by default, with Anderson's acceleration and
damping.

The functions given to KINSOL are the ones of mfem-mgis, which report
the failures instead of throwing through KINSOL (MFEM's functions always
report a success): the residual (a failure of the integration of the
behaviours lets KINSOL halve the step of Newton's method), the setup of
the linear solver, the resolution of the linear systems (a failure of the
linear solver is reported unless DiscardLinearSolverFailure), and the
product by the tangent operator (otherwise approximated by differences
of residuals, each one integrating the behaviours). The arrays of the
device of the vectors of SUNDIALS are synchronized after each write (a
direct solver on the host left them stale with --device cuda: null steps).

KINSOL stops on the maximum norm of the residual, relative to the
initial or reference residual; a null tolerance gives a fixed number of
iterations; the step criterion and the maximum Newton step of KINSOL,
which apply to the unknowns not scaled, are disabled by default
(ScaledStepTolerance, MaximumNewtonStep); a stagnation of the residual
below StagnationRelativeTolerance stops the resolution, accepted. The
initial residual is given to KINSOL without integrating the behaviours
again, and the behaviours are integrated again at the solution returned
when their last integration was made elsewhere. KINSOL 7.9 asks for a
setup at each iteration of Picard's method whatever its maximum number of
setup calls: the period of the updates is handled by the setup function.
